### Every API call in one file. Works in VS Code (extension "REST Client") and JetBrains IDEs (built in): click "Send Request" above a call.
### 1. Start the stack:  docker compose up      2. Put your admin key below (docker compose exec controlplane sh -c '. /secrets/env; echo $ControlPlane__AdminKey')
### 3. Run the calls from top to bottom; each one fills in the values the next one needs.

@ingest = http://localhost:8080
@admin = http://localhost:8081
@adminKey = PASTE_YOUR_ADMIN_KEY_HERE

### Health (no key needed)
GET {{ingest}}/healthz

###
GET {{admin}}/healthz

### 1. Create a customer (tenant)
# @name createTenant
POST {{admin}}/admin/v1/tenants
X-Admin-Key: {{adminKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Acme", "plan": "basic" }

###
@tenantId = {{createTenant.response.body.id}}

### 2. Create an API key for the customer (shown only once)
# @name createKey
POST {{admin}}/admin/v1/tenants/{{tenantId}}/api-keys
X-Admin-Key: {{adminKey}}

###
@apiKey = {{createKey.response.body.key}}

### 3. Register an endpoint (the demo receiver) and subscribe it to order.created (the secret is shown only once)
# @name createEndpoint
POST {{admin}}/admin/v1/tenants/{{tenantId}}/endpoints
X-Admin-Key: {{adminKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "url": "http://receiver:8080/webhook", "eventTypes": ["order.created"] }

###
@endpointId = {{createEndpoint.response.body.id}}
@secret = {{createEndpoint.response.body.secret}}

### 4. Give the demo receiver the signing secret so it can verify signatures
PUT http://localhost:9000/secret
Content-Type: text/plain

{{secret}}

### 5. SEND AN EVENT (this is the call your application makes)
POST {{ingest}}/v1/events
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: order-42-created

{ "type": "order.created", "data": { "orderId": 42, "amount": 1999 } }

### Same call again: you get the SAME eventId back (idempotency) and no second delivery

### 6. See what the receiver got
GET http://localhost:9000/received

### List the customer's endpoints and their event types
GET {{admin}}/admin/v1/tenants/{{tenantId}}/endpoints
X-Admin-Key: {{adminKey}}

### Change which events an endpoint receives
PUT {{admin}}/admin/v1/tenants/{{tenantId}}/endpoints/{{endpointId}}/subscriptions
X-Admin-Key: {{adminKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "eventTypes": ["order.created", "invoice.paid"] }

### Disable an endpoint (events are no longer routed to it)
PATCH {{admin}}/admin/v1/tenants/{{tenantId}}/endpoints/{{endpointId}}
X-Admin-Key: {{adminKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "disabled" }

### List API keys (prefixes only; the full key was shown once)
GET {{admin}}/admin/v1/tenants/{{tenantId}}/api-keys
X-Admin-Key: {{adminKey}}

### Suspend the customer (Ingest answers 403 tenant_suspended until set back to active)
PATCH {{admin}}/admin/v1/tenants/{{tenantId}}
X-Admin-Key: {{adminKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "suspended" }

### What an error looks like: a wrong API key gives 401
POST {{ingest}}/v1/events
Authorization: Bearer wgk_live_wrong
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "order.created", "data": {} }
